title: Conveyor belts
intro: A Conveyor lays belts on a grid and carries items along them, into and out of machines, with a crossing for workers and no code.

project: Empty | Belts

chapter: The belt | A Conveyor and its cells
create: Empty
rename: Line
add: Conveyor
explain: component:Conveyor | Conveyor | A Conveyor lays belts on the cells of the scene's tilemap, or world units without one, and carries items along them.
set: Conveyor.Belts = -4 0 right\n-3 0 right\n-2 0 right crossing\n-1 0 right\n0 0 right\n1 0 right\n2 0 right\n3 0 right
explain: field:Conveyor.Belts | Belts | Each row is a cell: its column and row, the way it carries, and crossing for one workers step over. A script lays a whole line at once with Lay Path.
set: Conveyor.Speed = 2
explain: field:Conveyor.Speed | Speed | Items move two cells a second, one to a cell, and wait when the cell ahead is full, so a full end backs the line up.
look: 0, 0, 5

chapter: Machines | A port out of one and into the next
deselect
create: Empty
rename: Maker
set: Transform.Position.X = -5
add: Inventory
set: Inventory.Items = Deck
editorset: Inventory.Items:count:1 = 6
add: ConveyorPort
set: ConveyorPort.Kind = Out
explain: component:ConveyorPort | Conveyor Port | An Out port puts what its machine holds on the belt leading away from it: six decks.
deselect
create: Empty
rename: Reader
set: Transform.Position.X = 4
add: Inventory
add: ConveyorPort
set: ConveyorPort.Items = Deck
set: ConveyorPort.Holds = 2
explain: field:ConveyorPort.Holds | Holds | An In port takes decks off the belt's end into the reader until it holds two, then leaves the next one waiting.

chapter: A worker | Belts are walls, crossings aren't
deselect
create: Grid Player
rename: Worker
set: Transform.Position = 0, -2, 0
set: GridMovement.Controllable = false
set: GridMovement.Destination = 0 -2
explain: field:GridMovement.Destination | Destination | The worker is sent across the line. The belts are solid, so it walks round to the crossing.

chapter: Play | Items, back-pressure and the crossing
play
wait: 3
expectat: Worker = 0, 2
say: The worker went over at the crossing and back along the other side.
wait: 4
expectvalue: Reader.Inventory.Items = Deck 2
expectvalue: Reader.ConveyorPort.Blocked = true
say: The reader took its two decks, and the other four wait on the belt behind it, a cell apart: its port is blocked, which a machine's lamp can show.
stop
say: Belts that run into another's side merge, taking turns, a split cell hands items round, and every line plays out the same at sixteen times speed.
